   **Conflicts:** [PCC2�?Ts default](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_pcc2.c:669) retains bytes already supplied from its register array while declining writes. [GD-ROM DMA�?Ts default](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_dreamcast_gdrom.c:1603) retains store-and-readback behavior for aligned unimplemented words: **6**. [dev_unreadable.c:41](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_unreadable.c:41) returns zero to request access failure; MIPS machine construction deliberately uses it for absent hardware: **5 where the architecture delivers it**.

   **My disposition:** 3 for LCA�?Ts catch-all: defined zero reads and discarded writes. There is no preexisting default-register storage or computed status answer here to preserve. Your `STAT0`/`STAT1` qualification is correct; their header declarations do not have matching cases.

The reporting precedents conflict too: PCC2 keys its default diagnostic by offset, GD-ROM by offset **and direction**, and SGI RE uses separate read/write flags for the entire unmatched region. �?oDisposition 3�?? alone therefore does not settle diagnostic granularity. Your GBE example also checks out: [get_rgb()](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_gbe.c:133) assigns all three components zero without printing.

**Q3 is confirmed by the call chain, not by its comments.** [tmp_alpha_tail.c:38](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/tmp_alpha_tail.c:38) instantiates `memory_rw.c` as `alpha_memory_rw` with `MEM_ALPHA`. In [memory_rw.c:595](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:595), device return zero becomes failure; with exceptions enabled, the branch invokes exception delivery only under `MEM_MIPS` and `MEM_M88K`, then returns `MEMORY_ACCESS_FAILED`.

Alpha�?Ts [load/store handlers](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_alpha_instr_loadstore.c:68) simply return on that failure. A failed ordinary load skips destination-register assignment. Their assertion that the translator �?oalready signalled a fault�?? is false for this path. The translator�?Ts own [failure comment](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_alpha.c:189) conversely promises the caller raises it; that is not implemented either.

Consequently, returning zero from LCA would abandon the access, not deliver an Alpha bus exception. Setting IOC status bits would also be distinct from CPU exception delivery. Disposition 5 requires that delivery work first.

For Q4, these are the candidate groups under the dispositions above:

| Round | Sites | Why they share�?"or must split |
|---|---|---|
| Interrupt stubs | 73, 85 | Same no-op callback contract. Implementing delivery changes the required observation. |
| PCI cycle decoding | 134 | Decoded routing and PCI responses; register readback alone cannot establish it. |
| Sparse lanes | 163 | Address/width-dependent byte forwarding and read placement; separate from decoding and stored values. |
| VALUE refusals | 206, 226, 241, 256, 280, 295 | Under uniform disposition 3, all share refusal-with-state-preservation and the same readback/diagnostic observation. |
| IOC default dispatch | 315, both directions | Undefined dispatch has zero-read/drop-write behavior, without an existing register value to preserve. |

Sharing a reporting helper does not make those different contracts one fix. If the VALUE round instead implements functionality, `IOC_CONF`�?Ts routing consumer and the TLB/window work require further splits. These are structural grouping candidates; I found no LCA reference in `regress/*.py`, so I cannot claim an existing test already discharges your reopening rule.

Two additional findings affect future choices:

- **Alpha interrupt delivery is also missing beyond LCA.** [Alpha�?Ts IRQ callbacks](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_alpha.c:215) only assign `irq_asserted`; the [execution-loop interrupt dispatch](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_dyntrans.c:206) has no Alpha branch. Forwarding LCA�?Ts callbacks to those setters would not complete disposition 7.
- The header identifies LCA�?Ts silently ignored base address as **`IOC_HAE`**, and names zero as **`IOC_W_MASK_1M`**. Thus another declared register already receives disposition 2, and the rejected zero window mask is also a named header encoding. [alpha_lcareg.h](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/thirdparty/alpha_lcareg.h:50).
